  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 through a series of molecular pathways involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C acts as a target for Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn targets the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1. This indicates a potential regulatory relationship where Ent-Gloeosteretriol modulates the activity of the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The presence of multiple paths with varying scores suggests that the interaction is consistent across different biological contexts, though the exact mechanism of Ent-Gloeosteretriol's influence on the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 remains partially understood. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a central mediator in the signaling cascade involving Oblonganoside C and the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1.",
